                    </div>
                    <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-12">
                        <h2 class="dept-heading">MECHANICAL ENGINEERING</h2>
                        <hr style="border:1px solid black;" />
                        <p class="dept-para">
                            B.Tech. in Mechanical Engineering program provides a comprehensive foundation in core mechanical engineering principles, covering areas such as thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, heat transfer, material science, dynamics, machine design, solid mechanics, and manufacturing processes. 
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="row mt-4">
                    <div class="col-12">
                        <p class="dept-para">
                            Students gain in-depth knowledge of mechanical systems and develop strong problem-solving and analytical skills through hands-on experience in labs, design projects, and industry internships. In addition to the foundational coursework, the program integrates emerging fields that reflect the rapid advancements in technology. Students explore cutting-edge topics such as robotics, automation, artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning (ML), 3D printing (additive manufacturing), smart materials, and sustainable energy systems. The curriculum also includes modern innovations like Industry 4.0 (smart manufacturing), IoT in mechanical systems, and renewable energy technologies. By combining traditional mechanical engineering with the latest technological trends, graduates are prepared to lead the development of intelligent, energy-efficient, and sustainable solutions across industries like automotive, aerospace, robotics, energy, and manufacturing.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

              

                <div class="row">
